Report - MongoDB for QA
========================

Loading Data into MongoDB
--------------------------
Two methods :
	1) Importing using query :
	mongoimport --db dbname --collection tablename --type csv --headerline --file filename
	2) Importing using Python code :
	import pandas as pd
	from pymongo import MongoClient

	df = pd.read_csv("filename", sep="|")

	client = MongoClient("mongodb://localhost:27017/")
	db = client["dbname"]

	db.tablename.insert_many(df.to_dict("records"))

Basic QA Checks
===================
Data Count :
----------------
	db.tablename.countDocuments()

Fieldname list :
-----------------
	Object.keys(db.tablename.findOne())

Find duplicates in a field :
---------------------------
	db.tablename.aggregate([
	  {
		$group: {
	  	_id: "$fieldname",
	  	count: { $sum: 1 }
		}
	  },
	  {
		$match: {
	  	count: { $gt: 1 }
		}
	  },
	  {
		$sort: {
	  	count: -1
		}
	  }
	])


Find count of null values in a field:
-------------------------------------
	db.tablename.countDocuments({
	    fieldname: {
		$exists: false,
		$nin: [null, "", NaN]
	    }
	})

Regex Validation:
-------------------
	Value Check :
	db.tablename.find({
	    fieldname: {
		$not: /^value$/
	    }
	})



	Email Validation :

	db.tablename.find({
		email: {
	    	$not: /^[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\.[A-Za-z]{2,}$/
		}
	})
	
Check Allowed Values :
--------------------
	db.tablename.find({
	    fieldname: {
		$nin: [
		    "value 1",
		    "value 2",
		    "value 3"
		]
	    }
	})

Business Rules : If promotion_description exists, promotion_price = selling_price
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

	db.tablename.find({
	    promotion_description: {
		$exists: true,
		$ne: ""
	    },
	    $expr: {
		$or: [
		    {
		        $ne: [
		            "$promotion_price",
		            "$selling_price"
		        ]
		    },
		    {
		        $ne: [
		            "$selling_price",
		            "$regular_price"
		        ]
		    }
		]
	    }
	})

Distinct Value Analysis:
------------------------
	db.tablename.distinct("fieldname")
	
Check Negative Prices:
----------------------
	db.tablename.find({
	    selling_price: {
		$lt: 0
	    }
	})
	
List out completely null fields
--------------------------------

	const coll = db.coop;   // replace with your collection name

	const totalDocs = coll.countDocuments();

	const sampleDoc = coll.findOne();

	for (const field in sampleDoc) {

	    const nonEmptyCount = coll.countDocuments({
		[field]: {
		    $nin: [null, "", NaN]
		}
	    });

	    if (nonEmptyCount === 0) {
